{"step_index":10843,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-25T16:18:50Z","thinking":"Successful matching triggers a success toast, followed by loading and displaying results. Otherwise, a failure toast indicates the matching process did not complete.\n\n\nInitial suspicion is that `data.stats` might be missing, requiring a check for its existence before loading results. Considering `data.process_id`, a call to a function that retrieves and loads all data associated with the process identifier could resolve potential data loading issues and ensure a fully populated results screen, which may involve waiting on the result before showing it. The user's Arabic feedback about the loading screen being full-screen versus on a menu screen necessitates re-examining how and where the loading screen is displayed during results population.\n\n\nThe user's feedback indicates a fundamental misunderstanding of the UI layout: the loading/result screen is incorrectly full-screen instead of occupying only the main content area alongside the menu. Examining screen dimensioning and synchronization is required. The UI elements need adjustment so that no element, particularly the matching button, is clipped or inaccessible.\n\n\nThe clipping issue of the start matching button suggests a layout problem stemming from window dimensions and screen sizing synchronization. Each screen's dimensions need careful adjustment to prevent content overflow and ensure no UI element is clipped, especially the matching button.\n\nThe loading screen's full-screen presentation violates the requirement for it to be scoped to the content area, which is likely caused by specific CSS rules. Examining the CSS rules in the `index.html` template will reveal if the root cause is with `.app-layout` or other style settings.\n\n\nThe `.main-content` CSS needs adjustment to ensure it properly occupies the remaining vertical space. Specifically, `height` and `max-height` should 