{"step_index":10849,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-25T16:19:17Z","thinking":"Examining the styling for potential causes of the clipped button and overflow issues. The `.main-content` class's `overflow-x: hidden !important;` declaration is a primary suspect. The `flex: 1` might be contributing to unexpected behavior. The `min-width` setting needs to be investigated as well.\n\n\nThe `flex: 1` property on `.screen` combined with the default `min-height: auto` led to incorrect height calculations. Vertical flex containers and their children both calculate minimum heights based on content, causing them to expand beyond their intended 100vh boundaries. The `overflow: hidden` on parent containers then masked the scrolling. The absence of `min-height: 0` on `.screen` and its parent ultimately caused the overflow issue.\n\n\nThe clipping occurred because the content exceeded the viewport, and the scrollbar was hidden due to the parent's `overflow: hidden`. The root cause is that flex container minimum heights were being incorrectly calculated. The proposed solution involves setting `height` and `max-height` to `100vh` on the `.app-layout`, `.sidebar`, and `.main-content` classes. Crucially, `.main-content` needs `min-height: 0` to allow it to shrink correctly within the flex layout. Also need to ensure `overflow-y:auto` for `.sidebar`.\n\n\nNow focusing on improving the visual layout for standard resolutions. Tightening up the vertical spacing in `#screen-new` should make the button immediately visible. Adjusting margins, padding, and font sizes within various sections to create a more compact and cleaner visual appearance. The goal is to optimize the screen for readability and accessibility across different devices without requiring scrolling.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"grep_search","args":{"CaseInsensitive":false,"MatchPerLine":true,"Query":"progress-modal","SearchPath":"D:/AI_Engineer/Pharmacy-agy-vision/desktop_app","toolAction":"Searching progress-modal occurrences","toolSummary":"Search progress-modal occurrences"}}]}
